Usage:
  nucleus shell [flags]
  nucleus shell -c <sql> [flags]
  nucleus shell [flags] < script.sql

Execute SQL against the configured database: one statement with -c, a script from stdin, or an interactive prompt on a terminal.

Flags:
  -c string
    	Shorthand for --command
  -command string
    	Execute one SQL command and exit
  -config string
    	Path to nucleus config file
  -database string
    	Database alias to use (defaults to database_default)
  -sandbox
    	Allow only read-only SQL statements
  -timeout duration
    	Per-statement timeout (default 10s)

Examples:
  nucleus shell --config nucleus.yml
  nucleus shell --config nucleus.yml -c "SELECT count(*) FROM users"
  nucleus shell --config nucleus.yml --sandbox < report.sql
